(5558734, 801855, 82036, '<td valign="top">should have been first.  It''s exposed well, composed well, and the depth of field is perfect.  I''m sure that gator is fairly lengthy and keeping him (her?) all in focus could be a challenge.  Instead, the tracks fall off 30-40 feet ahead and just in the foreground as well.  I''m not super crazy about vignetting but it was the smart play on this one.</td>', 'should have been first.  It''s exposed well, composed well, and the depth of field is perfect.  I''m sure that gator is fairly lengthy and keeping him (her?) all in focus could be a challenge.  Instead, the tracks fall off 30-40 feet ahead and just in the foreground as well.  I''m not super crazy about vignetting but it was the smart play on this one.', '2009-07-04 03:31:17.000000', NULL, 0),
