(5561371, 800800, 31352, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Judi:</b></div><hr/><i> I am sorry to see your DQ Susie.  I may be wrong but don''t cancer patients also lose their eyebrows along with their hair.  You chose a fantastic subject to photograph....if this had been Expert Editing rules this would have done well. When you look at a photo before editing, if you say that it is a photo of a girl with a skull cap on and then when you had finished the editing, you look at the result and say this is a girl.....then you have obviously removed the major element of the skull cap.  That is a general guideline for finding out if you have crossed the rules in your editing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>fair enough, the eyebrows are actually stuck on.. there not hers.. this photo was part of a shoot I did for a company who sells wigs, fakes eyelashes and eyebrows for with either cancer patients, drag queens, or crazy people like me hahaha I might actually post the whole series so you can see all the steps, becuase in the other shot she has no eyebrows..</td>', 'Originally posted by Judi: I am sorry to see your DQ Susie.  I may be wrong but don''t cancer patients also lose their eyebrows along with their hair.  You chose a fantastic subject to photograph....if this had been Expert Editing rules this would have done well. When you look at a photo before editing, if you say that it is a photo of a girl with a skull cap on and then when you had finished the editing, you look at the result and say this is a girl.....then you have obviously removed the major element of the skull cap.  That is a general guideline for finding out if you have crossed the rules in your editing.   fair enough, the eyebrows are actually stuck on.. there not hers.. this photo was part of a shoot I did for a company who sells wigs, fakes eyelashes and eyebrows for with either cancer patients, drag queens, or crazy people like me hahaha I might actually post the whole series so you can see all the steps, becuase in the other shot she has no eyebrows..', '2009-07-06 02:38:27.000000', NULL, 0),
